 "unknowns": ["whether the M01 launch calls the cinematic-mode pair is inferred, not traced: the cinematic flag 0x654120's only stores are the entry's set (0x450562) and the exit's clear (0x450f9b), and the per-frame camera dispatch (0x489cec) steps the cinematic camera 0x450ad0 exactly while the flag is set, so the intro's driven camera implies the pair ran; the mission opcode that activates the camera-mode object was not traced (docs/findings/2026-10-23-m01-fog-update-static.md section 4)", "whether the pair's fog object 0x71c2ac and the zone apply's 0x71c0b8 hold the same class-14 object is unknown (same finding, section 4)", "the far-clip half of the step (x4 in, x0.25 out) has no visible equivalent in this renderer: nothing drawn sits beyond the composed camera's 40 km far plane, so the factor changes no pixel", "the five-second clearing after hand-over is attributed to the aircraft flying through the constant ZONE1 fog (FOG_RANGES 1000 4500), which the owner frames' colours support and the image's lack of any fog interpolation requires; the original's per-frame fog reach was not measured at run time"],
 "review": {"identity": "Devin SWE-2/swe2-max-1 (implementer and reviewer are the same agent across resumed sessions, NOT independent)", "method": "Acceptance suite run locally with `retail,gpu,audio` (CS_GAME_DIR, CS_ENGINE_IMAGE): the owner's own command `cs --cs-path $CS_GAME_DIR --mission M01 --smoke-seconds 45 --capture-dir private/evidence/PARITY3-HAZE-FADE-AFTER-LAUNCH` drove the same windowed composition the owner plays on this machine's GPU — through the launch cinematic — and wrote real framebuffer PNGs plus report.json with its scripted checks passing: its `cinematic_end` frame shows the intro with the fog test off (the original's cinematic mode 0) and its `first_control`/`cinematic_handover` frames show the bound ZONE1 haze back on for the first controllable frame (mode 1). A second, no-teleport run (`--smoke-no-teleport`) flew the measured start pose continuously — never moving the player (`player_teleported:false`, `placements:[]`) — and wrote `flight_1s` beside `flight_5s`, the pair a few seconds apart that stands next to the owner's c03/c04: the haze thins as the aircraft closes on the terrain through the constant zone fog, which is the only behaviour the image supports since nothing in it interpolates fog parameters. The runs are automated, never `human_play`, and no original executable ran. This harness derives every field from the recorded log, production discovery of $CS_GAME_DIR, the smokes' reports and the hashes of those artifacts. LIMITS: the inference that the launch reaches the cinematic pair (the flag's only writers, the flag-gated cinematic camera step) is not a trace of the mission opcode, the far-clip half of the step draws no pixel here, and the thinning's attribution to flight through constant fog rests on the owner frames plus the absence of any interpolation code — no runtime fog reach was measured in the original. Validated with tools/validate_evidence.py (structure and artifact hashes, exit 0); --require-pass reports the recorded follow-up unknowns as unresolved issues, which stand as this task's honest limitations rather than being emptied to pass the gate."},
